<title>USA: United Defense wins Army minesweeper contract.</title>
<headline>United Defense wins Army minesweeper contract.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Army said Thursday it has awarded a $129 million contract to United Defense Ltd Partnership, Ground Systems Division, for the development of the Grizzly mine-clearing, obstacle breaching vehicle.</p>
<p>It said 80 percent of the work will be done at York, Pa., and 20 percent at Santa Clara, Calif. It is to be completed by April 30, 2001.</p>
